        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="48" height="48" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight"><a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author" class="text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a></p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">November 6, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="2.1k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">On the products below.</strong> We have not tested these mats.
          Sizes, thicknesses and materials were checked on 6 November 2026 against each mat's Amazon US
          listing and, where the listing did not give a figure, against the maker's site or at least two
          retailer listings. Where sources disagreed on a figure we left it out of the specification
          line. None of these figures are our own measurements. Prices are the Amazon prices we saw on
          that date; several mats come in more than one size, and prices change often, so check the size
          and price against the exact listing before ordering. We earn a commission if you buy through the
          Amazon links on this page; it does not change which products we list or what we say about them.
        </p>
